_v2_r1"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:14:09","kind":"goal_best","step":301056,"champion":"runs/ppo_v2_r1/champions/step_000301056.pt","check":{"score":681.692715641977,"laps":0.3125,"tiles":0.7716427156419905,"worst":195.97701149425413,"n":16},"run":"ppo_v2_r1","replay":"replays/ppo_v2_r1_0006.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:13:04","kind":"val_check","step":200704,"check":{"score":380.567167051796,"laps":0.125,"tiles":0.4756734170518043,"worst":47.65100671141343,"n":16},"run":"ppo_v2_r1"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:11:09","kind":"val_check","step":100352,"check":{"score":456.6692051730605,"laps":0.0,"tiles":0.5566692051730737,"worst":47.65100671141343,"n":16},"run":"ppo_v2_r1"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:11:09","kind":"goal_best","step":100352,"champion":"runs/ppo_v2_r1/champions/step_000100352.pt","check":{"score":456.6692051730605,"laps":0.0,"tiles":0.5566692051730737,"worst":47.65100671141343,"n":16},"run":"ppo_v2_r1","replay":"replays/ppo_v2_r1_0003.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:10:08","kind":"run_start","algo":"ppo","total_steps":6000000,"num_envs":8,"obs_dim":49,"run":"ppo_v2_r1"},{"t":"2026-11-10T21:10:08","kind":"stage_start","stage":"Learn the road","expect":"300-700 within 1-2M steps","step":0,"run":"ppo_v2_r1"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"Picked up again: the v1 agent was blind","text":"Reading the v1 code (Dec 2025) found three silent bugs. (1) The lidar read 0 on every ray: it looked for polygons in env.road, which holds Box2D bodies, so no point was ever 'on the road'. (2) 'Traction' was always 1: wheels have no ground_contact attribute (they keep a set of touched tiles), so the off-track penalty never fired. (3) The +500 finish bonus waited for info['finished_track'], a key CarRacing never sets (it says lap_finished). The agent saw only its speed and compass heading. Scored with CarRacing's own reward on 100 unseen tracks, the v1 best model averages -42.9 (best -7.6) and covers 6.5% of a track.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"Speed: 99% of a step was drawing a picture nobody looked at","text":"CarRacing draws its 96x96 state image inside every step(): 8.0 ms of a 9.4 ms step. Box2D's physics alone is 0.09 ms. Training now skips that drawing (videos still render), and a test checks the world stays bit-identical. The new lidar was chosen by a bake-off of six implementations (pure Python, NumPy, numba, C++, Rust, Go): all bit-identical on 900 poses x 19 rays; numba won (no build step, same source as the reference). A full env step is now ~0.5 ms.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"v2: new eyes, PPO, the real score","text":"New 49-number observation: speed, sideways slip, yaw rate, steer, which wheels are on the road, offset and heading against the centre line, 8 centre-line points up to 40 tiles ahead, and 19 lidar rays that work. Two-axis action (steer; gas or brake). Training reward = CarRacing's own score, so training aims at the metric; stage 1 stops hopeless episodes early (-50). PPO with observation and reward normalisation, time-limit bootstrapping. First run: validation 457 at 0.1 M steps.","kind":"journal"}]